       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there's a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation and arrhythmia. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nThe order may contain a typo. Common intended doses are 25 mg, 50 mg, 100 mg or 200 mg. If you tell me the intended dose, I can enter it right away, ideally confirmed by the prescribing clinician.\n\nOrders like this should also come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber, usually the treating physician or an authorized APP, and be reviewed by pharmacy. If a clinician does want an unusual dose, they should enter it themselves with a documented rationale."
