      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problem is patient safety, not authorization. A sertraline dose of 1000 mg daily is far above the 200 mg/day maximum and could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was a typo,** tell me the intended dose, such as 100 mg, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If a prescriber wants a dose this high,** they should enter and document it themselves. Pharmacy would also need to review it. I can't place it on a non-clinician's request.\n- **If the patient has taken a large amount of sertraline,** that is an overdose. It needs urgent clinical assessment and poison control, not a standing daily order.\n\nI can help with any of these."
      }
     ],
